From 6635a400307dc540c1bfe4ebb4712fc292dfcba4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 12:46:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] webui: the Traffic page says why it is empty in a bridging
 mode

rtrafd is deliberately not started outside a routing mode: start_rtraf()
returns at !is_routing_enabled() (sw_mode 2 and 3), and per-device accounting
off a conntrack table a bridging box never populates would report nothing
whatever it did. The page was silently blank on such a box, which reads as a
fault on a router that is working. It now shows a note naming the operation
mode. The decision reads sw_mode alone, the same value the daemon's own guard
reads; get_operation_mode() only supplies the name, and an unreadable sw_mode
shows no note rather than one that may be wrong.

RTRF_77 is the note's token, English-seeded in all 25 packs. RFW_318 ("open
Rule Status") is removed from all 25: nothing has referenced it since both Rule
Status links took RFW_290 in v3.1.7. Lockstep holds at 6987.

This is the page-note remainder of the rtrafd item under Open bugs in
docs/BACKLOG.md, which the v3.1.6 diag correction left unwritten.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
